e.\n- **Line 14 (`__VERIFIER_assert(!(g == 0));`)**: Can fail if `isr_2` runs after `isr_1` resets `g`.\n- **Line 15 (`g = 0;`)**: Executable.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nGiven the sequence and nature of operations, the reported atomicity violation involving lines 8, 15, and 9 is valid because:\n- `g` is written twice (`g = 1` and `g = 0`) with a read (`printf`) in between.\n- Interrupts can preempt causing interleaved execution.\n\nThus, the defect report is accurate.\n\n### Final Report\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 15, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 15, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
